  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge of high pressure will remain in place to\nthe west of the area on Monday, with 850mb temperatures \nremaining in the middle 20C across the area. The warm mid level \ntemperatures will result in a cap being in place across the area\non Monday, which will limit the shower and thunderstorm \npotential across the area. Highs will once again warm into the \nmiddle 90s to around 100 degrees on Monday. There may be \nslightly more mixing that occurs on Monday which could lower \ndewpoints during peak heating more than what occurs today. As a\nresult Heat index values of around 100 to 110 are expected on \nMonday. \n\nMonday night into Tuesday the ridge of high pressure starts to\nmove back to the west some. This will result in the area\nbecoming more in an upper level northwest flow pattern. Will \nhave to watch for convection developing to the northwest of the \narea Monday evening and night that could then move to the \nsoutheast. It is possible a weakening complex of showers and \nstorms pushes into portions of the area late Monday night into \nTuesday. The exact track will be dependent on where the \nconvection develops. If convection can make it into the area, \nslightly cooler temperatures will be possible on Tuesday as an \nincrease in clouds where any rain occurs. If the activity does \nnot move into the area or across portions of the area that are \nnot affect, the hotter temperatures will occur again on Tuesday.\n\nWarm overnight temperatures will also occur across the area \nearly this week as lows will only cool into the 70s each night \nthrough Tuesday night/Wednesday morning. A Heat Advisory remains\nin effect for the area from tonight through 7 PM Tuesday.\n\nThe upper level ridge of high pressure will remain further to\nthe west through late this week, leaving the region in an upper\nlevel northwest flow pattern. Some upper level disturbance will\nlikely ride the northwest flow and could bring some shower and\nthunderstorm potential to the area at times. There are still\nquestions on the exact track and timing of the disturbances and\njust how far south and to the west they track. \n\nThe ridge moving back to the west will also result in slightly\ncooler temperatures across the area. Highs closer to normal in \nthe upper 80s to the lower 90s are expected to occur across the\narea late this week.",
